{"surah": 113, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلْفَلَقِ ", "translation": "Say, \"I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَعُوذُ", "translit": "ُhdwُʿعَaʾ", "root": "عوذ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِرَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْفَلَقِ", "translit": "ِqَlَfْlٱ", "root": "فلق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ ", "translation": "From the evil of that which He created", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "شَرِّ", "translit": "ِّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خَلَقَ", "translit": "َqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ ", "translation": "And from the evil of darkness when it settles", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "شَرِّ", "translit": "ِّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "غَاسِقٍ", "translit": "ٍqِsāَغ", "root": "غسق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَقَبَ", "translit": "َbَqَw", "root": "وقب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَمِن شَرِّ ٱلنَّفَّٰثَٰتِ فِى ٱلْعُقَدِ ", "translation": "And from the evil of the blowers in knots[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "شَرِّ", "translit": "ِّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّفَّٰثَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰhtَّٰfَّnlٱ", "root": "نفث"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعُقَدِ", "translit": "ِdَqُʿعْlٱ", "root": "عقد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ ", "translation": "And from the evil of an envier when he envies.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "شَرِّ", "translit": "ِّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَاسِدٍ", "translit": "ٍdِsāَḥ", "root": "حسد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَسَدَ", "translit": "َdَsَḥ", "root": "حسد"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "قال من صلى ليلة الأربعاء ركعتين يقرأ في الأول فاتحة الكتاب وقل أعوذ برب الفلق عشر مرات وفي الثانية بعد الفاتحة قل أعوذ برب الناس عشر مرات", "english": "**Regarding the Day of Saturday:** Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays on the day of Saturday four rakʿahs, reciting in each rakʿah Fātiḥat al-Kitāb once and {«قل هو الله أحد»} three times — then when he finishes, he recites Āyat al-Kursī — Allah writes for him for every letter a Ḥajj and an ʿUmrah, and raises for him for every letter the reward of a year of fasting its days and standing (in prayer) its nights. And Allah — Mighty and Majestic — gives him for every letter the reward of a martyr, and he will be beneath the shade of the Throne of Allah with the Prophets and the martyrs.\"", "book_title": "Arrangement of Litanies", "section_title_ar": "Section 160", "section_title_en": "The Book of Invocations and Supplications — Section on Virtues of Voluntary Prayers for Specific Days and Nights", "section_index": 160, "anchors": "- Root: ركع (rakaʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To bow, to incline the body; the specific posture of bowing in prayer\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used both for the specific ritual posture in prayer and metaphorically for humility and submission before Allah\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) — the physical bowing in prayer; the term \"rakʿah\" (unit of prayer) derives from the bowing within it\n- Root: احد (aḥad)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: One, unique; the root denoting oneness and singularity\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological context, refers to Allah's absolute oneness as expressed in Surah Al-Ikhlāṣ {«قل هو الله أحد»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Used in the Quranic context of divine unity, distinguishing Allah's unique essence from all creation\n- Root: ليل (layl)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Night; the period of darkness from sunset to dawn\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The night is a time of worship and devotion; Allah says {«ومن الليل فتهجد به نافلة لك»}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — the night as a temporal designation for specific voluntary prayers\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The syntactic structure of conditional clauses (من صلى... كان له) follows the pattern of protasis and apodosis, where the reward clause is grammatically linked to the condition through the prepositional phrase", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Arrangement of Litanies'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "2": [{"arabic": "يجاوزهن بر ولا فاجر من شر ما خلق فإذا جن عليه الليل يقول يا أرض ربي وربك الله أعوذ بالله من شرك وشر ما فيك وشر ما دب عليك أعوذ بالله من شر كل أسد وأسود وحية وعقرب ومن شر ساكن البلد ووالد وما ولد وله ما سكن في الليل والنهار وهو السميع العليم السابعة في الحراسة ينبغي أن يحتاط بالنهار فلا يمشي منفردا خارج القافلة لأنه ربما يغتال أو ينقطع ويكون بالليل متحفظا عند النوم فإن نام في ابتداء الليل افترش ذراعه وإن نام في آخر الليل نصب ذراعه نصبا وجعل رأسه في كفه هكذا كان ينام رسول الله ص", "english": "He ought to seek out a righteous companion, one who loves goodness and assists in it: if he forgets, the companion reminds him; if he remembers, the companion aids him; if he fears, the companion emboldens him; if he weakens, the companion strengthens him; if his breast narrows, the companion enlarges his patience. He should bid farewell to his resident companions, his brothers, and his neighbors — taking leave of them and seeking their supplications, for God Most High places goodness in their prayers. The Sunnah of farewell is to say: «أستودع الله دينك وأمانتك وخواتيم عملك» — \"I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the seal of your deeds.\" And he, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say to one intending travel: \"In God's protection and His care — may God provide you with piety, forgive your sin, and direct you toward goodness wherever you may be.\"", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 199", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Etiquette of Travel — Section 199: On the Comprehensive Etiquette of the Journey (From Provisioning to Guarding)", "section_index": 199, "anchors": "- Root: س ف ر (S-F-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"السفر: كشف الغطاء\" — unveiling, uncovering; the traveler is one who uncovers the veils of distant lands.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"السفر: كشف الغطاء، ويختص ذلك بالأعيان\" — the journey is a literal uncovering of horizons, yet the spiritual journey unveils the soul's veils.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Haqiqah: \"سافر سفرا بعيدا\" (to travel far); Majaz: \"وجه مسفر: مشرق سرورا\" — a face radiant with joy, as the traveler's face brightens with divine trust.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — governing the permissible separation between the preposition and its object for rhetorical emphasis, as in the supplications' structural pauses.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "3": [{"arabic": "وفي نوادر التفسير عن ابن عباس رضي الله عنهما {ومن شر غاسق إذا وقب} قال قيام الذكر وهذه يلية غالبة إذا هاجت لا يقاومها عقل ولا دين وهي مع أنها صالحة لأن تكون باعثة على الحياتين كما سبق فهي أقوى آلة الشيطان على بني آدم وإليه أشار صلى الله عليه وسلم بقوله ما رأيت من ناقصات عقل ودين أغلب لذوي الألباب منكن (1) وإنما ذلك لهيجان الشهوة وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم في دعائه اللهم إني أعوذ بك من شر سمعي وبصري وقلبي وشر مني (2) وقال أسألك أن تطهر قلبي وتحفظ فرجي (3) فما يستعيذ منه رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم كيف يجوز التساهل فيه لغي", "english": "وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم: \"لا يلقى الله أحد بذنب أعظم من جهالة أهله.\"", "book_title": "Harms of the Tongue", "section_title_ar": "Section 296", "section_title_en": "Section 296", "section_index": 296, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Harms of the Tongue'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 829], [2, 829, 1917], [3, 1917, 2733], [4, 2733, 3711]], "2": [[1, 250, 824], [2, 824, 1671], [3, 1671, 2417], [4, 2417, 3365]], "3": [[1, 350, 1160], [2, 1160, 1842], [3, 1842, 2998], [4, 2998, 3900], [5, 3900, 4756]], "4": [[1, 350, 1161], [2, 1161, 1845], [3, 1845, 4002], [4, 4002, 4581], [5, 4581, 5670]], "5": [[1, 350, 1170], [2, 1170, 1861], [3, 1861, 2986], [4, 2986, 3900], [5, 3900, 4651]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 350, 1163], [2, 1163, 3011], [3, 3011, 4397], [4, 4397, 6060]], "2": [[1, 350, 1248], [2, 1248, 2573], [3, 2573, 3741], [4, 3741, 5224]], "3": [[1, 350, 1653], [2, 1653, 2752], [3, 2752, 4614], [4, 4614, 6066], [5, 6066, 7444]], "4": [[1, 400, 1678], [2, 1678, 2755], [3, 2755, 6155], [4, 6155, 7068], [5, 7068, 8785]], "5": [[1, 400, 1720], [2, 1720, 2833], [3, 2833, 4644], [4, 4644, 6115], [5, 6115, 7322]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 330, 806], [2, 806, 2094], [3, 2094, 2906], [4, 2906, 3890]], "2": [[1, 160, 720], [2, 720, 1546], [3, 1546, 2582], [4, 2582, 3520]], "3": [[1, 10, 1023], [2, 1023, 1702], [3, 1702, 3118], [4, 3118, 4270], [5, 4270, 5330]], "4": [[1, 30, 1174], [2, 1174, 1941], [3, 1941, 4457], [4, 4457, 5133], [5, 5133, 6380]], "5": [[1, 80, 1108], [2, 1108, 1797], [3, 1797, 3175], [4, 3175, 4343], [5, 4343, 5090]]}, "mah": [{"word": "قل", "start": 0.031, "end": 1.273}, {"word": "أعوذ", "start": 2.595, "end": 3.256}, {"word": "برب", "start": 3.357, "end": 4.058}, {"word": "الفلق", "start": 4.098, "end": 5.38}, {"word": "من", "start": 5.52, "end": 6.662}, {"word": "شر", "start": 6.682, "end": 7.143}, {"word": "ما", "start